00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:02.880
that logic. The four-year having cycle

00:02:00.399 --> 00:02:05.200
was the gospel of crypto for over a

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.600
decade. Every four years, Bitcoin's

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:09.759
mining reward gets cut in half. Less new

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:12.239
supply enters the market. If demand

00:02:09.759 --> 00:02:14.239
stays the same or grows, price goes up.

00:02:12.239 --> 00:02:17.280
Simple economics. And it worked. In

00:02:14.239 --> 00:02:19.360
2012, 2016, and 2020, after every

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:21.280
having, Bitcoin went on a massive bull

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:23.680
run within the following 12 to 18

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:26.000
months. Then it crashed. Then it slowly

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:28.720
recovered, rinse and repeat. So,

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:31.360
everyone expected 2025, the year after

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:33.519
the April 24 having, to be the golden

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:36.400
year, the blowoff top, the euphoric

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:38.720
peak. Instead, 2025 was the first

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:41.360
negative post-h having year in Bitcoin's

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:43.120
entire history. Let that sink in. The

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:46.000
pattern that everybody built their

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:48.239
entire investment thesis around just

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:50.720
broke for the first time ever. And

00:02:48.239 --> 00:02:52.879
here's my take. The four-year cycle was

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:54.720
never actually about the having. It just

00:02:52.879 --> 00:02:57.120
happened to coincide with something

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:59.120
else. And that something else is what's

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.040
really been driving Bitcoin the entire

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:04.000
time. Let me explain. Think about what

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:06.800
Bitcoin looked like in 2012 or 2016.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:08.720
There were no institutions, no ETFs, no

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:10.879
sovereign nations were buying it. There

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:12.560
were maybe a few thousand altcoins in

00:03:10.879 --> 00:03:14.640
total. It was really just retail

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:17.280
investors, regular people like you and

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:19.280
me buying and holding actual Bitcoin.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:22.000
And when the having cut news supply in

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:24.239
half, it created a real supply shock

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:26.319
because miners were a huge percentage of

00:03:24.239 --> 00:03:28.800
the daily selling pressure. When their

00:03:26.319 --> 00:03:31.280
rewards got cut, there was genuinely

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:33.760
less Bitcoin hitting the market. Demand

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:36.159
didn't change. Supply dropped. Price

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:38.879
went up. Basic stuff, right? But look at

00:03:36.159 --> 00:03:41.840
where we are now. As of February 2025,

00:03:38.879 --> 00:03:44.799
over 120 million unique tokens have been

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:47.519
created. For context, fewer than 3,000

00:03:44.799 --> 00:03:50.959
tokens were created between 2017 and

00:03:47.519 --> 00:03:53.599
2018, and fewer than 500 between 2013

00:03:50.959 --> 00:03:56.000
and 2014. Today, we probably have well

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:58.080
over 120 million. The market is

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:00.720
completely oversaturated with altcoins.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:04.319
As of early 2026, Black Rockck's Bitcoin

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:06.959
ETF alone holds roughly 765,000

00:04:04.319 --> 00:04:10.080
Bitcoin, worth nearly 54 billion.

00:04:06.959 --> 00:04:11.840
Strategy owns over 714,000 Bitcoin,

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:13.599
making it the largest corporate holder

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:16.400
of Bitcoin. Countries like China,

00:04:13.599 --> 00:04:18.479
Ukraine, the UK, El Salvador, amongst a

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:20.880
couple of others, have direct exposure

00:04:18.479 --> 00:04:23.520
to Bitcoin. And the US now has

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:25.680
established a strategic Bitcoin reserve.

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:28.639
So this is not a retail-driven market

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:31.120
anymore. Institutional buyers now absorb

00:04:28.639 --> 00:04:33.919
more Bitcoin than miners produce. Let me

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:36.639
say that again. Institutions are buying

00:04:33.919 --> 00:04:38.720
more Bitcoin annually than the total

00:04:36.639 --> 00:04:40.320
amount of Bitcoin being mined. The

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:42.320
having used to be the single most

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:44.240
important event in Bitcoin. And now it's

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:46.160
just a date in the calendar. It's not

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:48.080
driving the market anymore. What's now

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:50.720
driving the market is institutional

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:53.120
demand, the business cycle, interest

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:54.800
rates, and global liquidity. And this is

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:56.720
the part that nobody wants to talk

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:58.880
about. Bitcoin's entire value

00:04:56.720 --> 00:05:00.960
proposition was built on one thing.

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:03.360
There will only ever be 21 million

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:05.120
coins. Absolute scarcity, right? If you

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:06.880
wanted exposure to Bitcoin's price, you

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:09.199
had to buy one of those 21 million

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:11.520
coins. Every buyer removed supply from

00:05:09.199 --> 00:05:13.600
the market. Every holder added scarcity

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:16.160
pressure. That is what made the having

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:18.320
cycle work. But derivatives changed that

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:20.960
game completely. Futures, options,

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:23.440
perpetual swaps, leverage ETFs. These

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:25.759
instruments let investors bet on

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:28.320
Bitcoin's price without ever touching or

00:05:25.759 --> 00:05:30.240
owning the actual asset. Think about

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:32.639
what that means for a minute. The number

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:34.639
of actual Bitcoin is capped at 21

00:05:32.639 --> 00:05:36.320
million, but the number of derivative

00:05:34.639 --> 00:05:38.720
contracts that can be created is

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:41.199
infinite. There is no cap on how many

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:42.800
paper contracts can exist. So now you

00:05:41.199 --> 00:05:44.720
have a situation where capital that

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:47.280
would have previously flowed into buying

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:50.080
and holding real Bitcoin, driving up

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:52.160
value through a supply shock is instead

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:53.840
getting diverted into high leverage

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:55.680
betting. Investors can make

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:57.840
significantly more money through

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:00.000
leverage derivatives than by simply

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:02.240
owning the coin. So that is where the

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.960
money goes. And this does something very

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:07.759
specific to the market. It decouples

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:10.080
price from scarcity. See in the old days

00:06:07.759 --> 00:06:12.400
more demand meant more buying, right?

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:15.759
which meant less available supply which

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:18.000
meant higher prices. Now more demand can

00:06:15.759 --> 00:06:20.639
be satisfied entirely through paper

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:23.199
contracts. The demand gets met without a

00:06:20.639 --> 00:06:24.800
single Bitcoin actually changing hands.

00:06:23.199 --> 00:06:26.960
This is why we saw the largest

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:29.840
liquidation event in crypto history in

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:32.000
October of 25. And it's why 9 billion in

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:33.759
leveraged positions got wiped out in a

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:35.520
single week in February. And these

00:06:33.759 --> 00:06:37.919
aren't long-term holders selling their

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:40.160
Bitcoin. These are derivative positions

00:06:37.919 --> 00:06:42.240
getting blown up. leveraged bets

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:44.400
completely unwinding. The scarcity of

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:46.479
the actual asset doesn't prevent these

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:48.720
crashes. When the leverage supporting

00:06:46.479 --> 00:06:51.120
these paper positions evaporates, the

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:53.759
price drops regardless of how many coins

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:56.160
actually exist. The 21 million cap still

00:06:53.759 --> 00:06:58.400
matters longterm, but right now

00:06:56.160 --> 00:07:00.800
derivatives are diluting its impact on

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:02.880
price action in a very real way. So, if

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:05.120
the having isn't driving price anymore,

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:06.800
then what is? Well, we talked about it a

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:09.120
minute ago. Global liquidity is the

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:11.360
first thing. Raul Pal, one of the most

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:14.080
respected macro investors in the world,

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:17.199
puts it really simply. Global liquidity

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:19.120
explains 90% of the moves in Bitcoin.

00:07:17.199 --> 00:07:21.360
So, let me break it down for you. Global

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:23.919
liquidity is essentially how much money

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:26.319
is available in the financial system.

00:07:23.919 --> 00:07:28.880
It's measured by the global M2 money

00:07:26.319 --> 00:07:31.280
supply, which tracks cash, checking

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:33.440
deposits, savings, money market

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:36.000
accounts, and similar instruments across

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:38.479
all major economies. When central banks

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:41.360
print money, cut interest rates, or

00:07:38.479 --> 00:07:43.840
loosen regulation, then liquidity goes

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:45.840
up. More money in the system means more

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:48.720
capital flowing into risk assets.

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:51.120
Bitcoin is largely traded as a high-risk

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:53.280
asset. When liquidity contracts, when

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:55.039
the Fed tightens and governments drain

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:57.840
their accounts and the dollar

00:07:55.039 --> 00:08:00.400
strengthens, then Bitcoin and other risk

00:07:57.840 --> 00:08:02.560
assets suffer. It doesn't matter how

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:04.479
scarce the asset is. If there's no

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:06.319
available capital to bid up the price,

00:08:04.479 --> 00:08:08.479
the price doesn't go up. According to

00:08:06.319 --> 00:08:11.120
research from Lyn Alden, Bitcoin moves

00:08:08.479 --> 00:08:13.440
in the direction of global liquidity 83%

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:15.199
of the time over any 12-month period.

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:17.680
That is higher than any other major

00:08:15.199 --> 00:08:20.160
asset class. Bitcoin is quite literally

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:22.080
a liquidity barometer. Now, overlay that

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:25.680
with what happened throughout most of

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:27.599
2024 and 2025, manufacturing was in

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:29.919
contraction. The ISM, which is the

00:08:27.599 --> 00:08:31.440
manufacturing index, which measures

00:08:29.919 --> 00:08:33.519
essentially the health of the business

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:36.399
cycle, whether it's contracting or

00:08:33.519 --> 00:08:38.640
expanding, spent 10 consecutive months

00:08:36.399 --> 00:08:41.279
below 50, meaning the economy was

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:44.240
contracting. In December 2025, it hit

00:08:41.279 --> 00:08:48.880
47.9. But here's what just happened. In

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:50.399
January of 2026, the ISM jumped to 52.6.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:54.160
For reference, the last time it was

00:08:50.399 --> 00:08:56.560
above 52 was September of 2022, and it

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:59.680
hasn't been above 50 in over a year. So,

00:08:56.560 --> 00:09:01.200
the economy just flipped to expansion.

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:03.440
And this is a chart that I want you to

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:06.080
really pay attention to. When the ISM is

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:07.519
above 50, we are in economic expansion.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:10.320
When it's below 50, we're in

00:09:07.519 --> 00:09:12.959
contraction. Now, if you overlay the ISM

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:15.200
with Bitcoin's price history, there is a

00:09:12.959 --> 00:09:18.160
very strong correlation. We have never

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:20.720
had a sustained bare market in Bitcoin

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:22.720
while the ISM is above 50 and trending

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:24.800
higher. The business cycle and global

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:26.640
liquidity, not the having cycle, are

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:28.480
what matter now. And there's a third

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:30.640
piece to this that's just as important,

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:32.720
and that's interest rates. The interest

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:35.279
rate environment is far more indicative

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:37.680
of what Bitcoin will do than any having

00:09:35.279 --> 00:09:40.320
countdown. When the Fed cuts rates,

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:42.880
liquidity flows in. Risk assets like

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:45.360
Bitcoin rally. When the Fed tightens,

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:48.240
risk assets fall, Bitcoin falls, and

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:51.040
risk off assets like gold and silver and

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:53.200
everything go through the roof, which is

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:55.200
exactly what we've all seen play out

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:57.200
over the last couple of months. And this

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:59.760
is exactly what played out when Bitcoin

00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:01.760
peaked in October of 2025. What else

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:03.839
happened around this time? Well, markets

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:06.160
started pricing in that Kevin Worsh,

00:10:03.839 --> 00:10:08.800
Trump's nominee to replace Jerome Pal as

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:11.760
Fed chair, would potentially bring a

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:14.560
hawkish approach. tighter balance sheet,

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:16.160
potentially higher rates for longer, and

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:18.399
the minute that the market sniffed

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:20.320
tighter monetary conditions, Bitcoin

00:10:18.399 --> 00:10:22.240
sold off, not because of the having

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:25.120
cycle and not because of any

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:28.079
cryptospecific event. The US has roughly

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:30.640
8 trillion in debt to roll over in 2026.

00:10:28.079 --> 00:10:32.480
Now, that debt has to get refinanced and

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:34.079
that requires liquidity. And when

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:36.000
governments need to manage that kind of

00:10:34.079 --> 00:10:38.000
debt load, they historically have to

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:39.760
debase the currency, which means

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:41.440
printing more money. Now, China's

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:43.680
already accelerated money printing to

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:45.920
stimulate growth. Banking regulations

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:47.760
are being loosened to allow banks to buy

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:49.839
more government bonds with leverage,

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:52.160
which effectively creates money. The

00:10:49.839 --> 00:10:54.959
liquidity is coming. It always does. The

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:56.320
question really is when and not if. Now,

00:10:54.959 --> 00:10:58.320
this might shift your thinking a little

00:10:56.320 --> 00:10:59.839
bit. So, go back and look at the last

00:10:58.320 --> 00:11:03.360
couple of bull runs. We can look at

00:10:59.839 --> 00:11:05.360
2013, 2017, 2021. What was happening

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:07.839
with global liquidity during each of

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:10.079
those periods of time? It was expanding

00:11:07.839 --> 00:11:12.399
every single time. The h havingings just

00:11:10.079 --> 00:11:14.640
happened to coincide with periods of

00:11:12.399 --> 00:11:16.720
global monetary expansion. The having

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:19.040
was a convenient narrative that fit the

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:22.160
timeline. The 2020 bull market wasn't

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:24.640
driven by the having. The 2020 to 2021

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:26.880
bull market wasn't driven by the having.

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:29.279
It was driven by the largest liquidity

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:31.519
injection in modern history. The Fed's

00:11:29.279 --> 00:11:34.079
response to what we all know to be CO.

00:11:31.519 --> 00:11:36.640
Same with 2024's rally. The having

00:11:34.079 --> 00:11:38.720
happened in April of 2024, but Bitcoin

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:40.959
had already hit all-time highs before

00:11:38.720 --> 00:11:42.720
the having even occurred because ETF

00:11:40.959 --> 00:11:44.320
inflows were flooding the market with

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:46.480
demand that had nothing to do with

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:48.800
mining supply. There's an argument to be

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:51.200
made that Bitcoin was never really on a

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:53.760
4-year having cycle and it was always on

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:55.519
a liquidity cycle. The havingss just

00:11:53.760 --> 00:11:57.600
happened to overlap. And now that

00:11:55.519 --> 00:12:00.240
institutions, derivatives, and macro

00:11:57.600 --> 00:12:02.480
forces dominate the market, the overlap

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:04.560
has broken. If anything, we may be

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:06.959
looking at something closer to a 5-year

00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:08.959
cycle now. Not based on havingss, but

00:12:06.959 --> 00:12:11.760
based on the global debt refinancing

00:12:08.959 --> 00:12:13.839
cycle, the ISM business cycle and

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:15.680
interest rate regimes. So, what do you

00:12:13.839 --> 00:12:17.920
actually do with all this information?

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:20.079
Well, first you stop watching the having

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:22.240
countdown clock because it's probably a

00:12:20.079 --> 00:12:25.279
distraction. You start watching global

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:26.959
liquidity, the ISM, the interest rates.

00:12:25.279 --> 00:12:28.720
Those are the signals that actually

00:12:26.959 --> 00:12:30.720
predict where Bitcoin is going in my

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:32.320
opinion. Second, understand what's

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:35.200
happening right now. Bitcoin just

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:38.480
dropped nearly 50% from its high. Fear

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:40.880
is at historic extremes. ETFs are seeing

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:43.200
outflows and headlines are screaming

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:45.040
that it's all over. But the ISM just

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:47.760
flipped above 50 for the first time in

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:50.560
over a year. And it hasn't been over 52

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:52.480
since September of 2022. The US

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:54.240
government has 8 trillion in debt that

00:12:52.480 --> 00:12:56.720
they have to refinance, which will

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:59.120
require liquidity. Central banks

00:12:56.720 --> 00:13:01.120
globally are loosening conditions.

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:03.120
Bernstein, one of Wall Street's most

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:05.200
respected research firms, is calling

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:07.040
this the weakest bare market in

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:10.480
Bitcoin's history and is still

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:13.279
projecting 150,000 by the end of 2026.

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:15.839
They point out that unlike 2022, there's

00:13:13.279 --> 00:13:18.079
no fraud, no exchange collapse, and

00:13:15.839 --> 00:13:20.880
really no systematic failure at all.

00:13:18.079 --> 00:13:22.720
This is a macrodriven correction, not a

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:24.880
structural breakdown. That doesn't mean

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:27.360
the bottom is in. It could go lower. It

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:29.200
can always go lower, but it means the

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:30.880
setup for what comes next is

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:34.000
fundamentally different from what the

00:13:30.880 --> 00:13:36.480
fear headlines suggest. Third, own the

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:38.560
asset. Stop betting on the asset or

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:40.959
using leverage. The lesson from the

00:13:38.560 --> 00:13:42.959
derivatives explosion is clear. Capital

00:13:40.959 --> 00:13:45.600
flowing into paper contracts doesn't

00:13:42.959 --> 00:13:47.920
support Bitcoin's price the way actual

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:50.480
ownership does. If you believe in the

00:13:47.920 --> 00:13:52.560
long-term thesis, own the real Bitcoin.

00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:55.120
Stop overleveraging yourself and trading

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:57.440
it. And fourth, stop listening to people

00:13:55.120 --> 00:14:00.079
who are still using a 2016 playbook for

00:13:57.440 --> 00:14:01.920
the 2026 market. The game has completely

00:14:00.079 --> 00:14:04.079
changed. The players have changed. The

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:06.320
drivers have changed. Your framework

00:14:04.079 --> 00:14:08.480
needs to change also. And if you agree

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:10.720
with this thesis, then the best way to

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:13.680
expose yourself is to stop focusing on

00:14:10.720 --> 00:14:16.000
what all the news is saying and just

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:18.000
dollar cost average over a long period

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:19.519
of time. Look, I know the headlines are

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:21.360
scary right now, but if you actually

00:14:19.519 --> 00:14:23.040
understand what drives this market,

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:24.959
liquidity, the business cycle, and

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:26.240
interest rates, the picture looks a lot

00:14:24.959 --> 00:14:28.399
different than what the media is telling

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:30.560
you. The four-year cycle is dead. But

00:14:28.399 --> 00:14:32.320
Bitcoin isn't. Not even close. Not if

00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:33.839
you ask me. If this gave you a new way

00:14:32.320 --> 00:14:35.120
of thinking about Bitcoin, hit the

00:14:33.839 --> 00:14:36.720
subscribe button. It would mean the

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:38.480
world to me. Share this with somebody

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:40.399
who needs to hear it. And drop a comment

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:42.320
down below. Do you think the four-year

00:14:40.399 --> 00:14:43.760
cycle is really over or is it just

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:46.480
evolving? And I look forward to seeing

00:14:43.760 --> 00:14:46.480
you in a future

